==Trivia==
*The trifecta of Moskandag, [[Magellanic (Cats of the Cosmos)|Magellanic]] and [[Buutara (Cats of the Cosmos)|Buutara]] all reference [[wikipedia:Space Battleship Yamato|''Space Battleship Yamato'']]:
**Buutara's name in Japanese (ブータラ星 Būtara-sei) is spelled similarly to that of the planet and solar system Beemela (ビーメラ星 Bīmera-sei), and on the map it looks like the head of one of the humanoid insects that inhabit [[wikia:yamato:Beemela 4|Beemela 4]].
**Moskandag's name in Japanese (モスカンダグ Mosukandagu) is spelled almost the same as that of the planet [[wikia:yamato:Iscandar|Iscandar]] (イスカンダル Isukandaru), which is located in the [[wikia:yamato:Large Magellanic Cloud|Large '''Magellanic''' Cloud]] and once sent a mission to Beemela 4.
***Moskandag's Treasure, Hope, references Iscandar's role throughout the series, and the person on its enemy base looks similar to [[wikipedia:Takuya Kimora|Takuya Kimora]]'s portrayal of [[wikia:yamato:Susumu Kodai|Susumu Kodai]] in the [[wikia:yamato:Space Battleship Yamato (live action film)|2010 live-action movie]].
***The two kana in Moskandag's Japanese name that aren't in Iscandar's are モ Mo and グ gu; if you combine these two characters, you get モグ Mogu, which sounds very close to the main threat [[Corporal Weyland]]'s Japanese name, Captain Moguu (キャプテン・モグー).

